WEBVTT

00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:06.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Monday the twenty-eighth. Everyone on? Bit of an echo from somewhere.</v>

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:17.309
<v Hannah Price>That's probably me. There, headset in. I was going to ask about weekend plans, then remembered it's Monday. Mine were a washout anyway, with that weather.</v>

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.739
<v Jamie Brennan>Same. Put the washing out, brought the washing in. Full itinerary.</v>

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:27.230
<v David Whitfield>Better entertainment than the football last night. Ninety minutes I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:29.239 --> 00:00:31.339
<v Tomasz Nowak>You say that every Monday, though.</v>

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:38.460
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, just connected. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous. More time sitting there than actually driving.</v>

00:00:38.979 --> 00:00:43.530
<v Sarah Okafor>You're here now. Right, let's separate what's finished from what we're actually agreeing.</v>

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:51.429
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I signed off the inspection on the relief valve on Tuesday. That's done, not something still on my list.</v>

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.950
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, closed item.</v>

00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:02.950
<v Hannah Price>And I signed off the inspection on the fire alarm panel on Tuesday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.290
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, so the inspection isn't still outstanding?</v>

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:11.769
<v Hannah Price>No, inspection signed off. Just clearing that up.</v>

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:20.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, we already swapped the filter on the turbine one gas valve yesterday. Don't carry that forward as another job.</v>

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:23.640
<v David Whitfield>Yep, understood. Old line, not new work.</v>

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:34.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel tomorrow at 9:30? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:01:35.629 --> 00:01:41.579
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel tomorrow at 9:30. First priority, understood.</v>

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:50.319
<v Fiona Doyle>So that stays at the top because of the production hold, rather than just sitting with the routine stuff?</v>

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Needs doing first, and the sign-off is tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:05.459
<v David Whitfield>While we're on plant status, I saw the pressure on the stretch wrapper dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:09.039
<v Tomasz Nowak>Came back without anyone touching it?</v>

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.120
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Just an observation, I'm not putting a job against it.</v>

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:21.810
<v Jamie Brennan>Similar sort of thing from me: heard a slight rattle from the forklifts. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both observations. Neither's a new task out of this meeting.</v>

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:32.840
<v Fiona Doyle>And we're still waiting on parts for the GT1. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:40.229
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, that's the blocker. Can't do much with an empty space where the parts should be.</v>

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.659
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. Blocked, not available work for today.</v>

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:48.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. What else have we got on the safety side?</v>

00:02:50.439 --> 00:02:58.490
<v Hannah Price>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon. Not an emergency but don't let it slip — that's where I'd put it.</v>

00:02:59.699 --> 00:03:03.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah Price. Monthly fire alarm test with you this afternoon, then.</v>

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.430
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll do it. Routine, but it isn't getting pushed out.</v>

00:03:10.719 --> 00:03:14.919
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, talking over you — that's separate from the inspection you mentioned?</v>

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.800
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, separate. Tuesday's inspection is finished; this is the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon.</v>

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:27.159
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you also update the risk assessment for work on the Palletiser? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.930
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Palletiser. Normal priority, that's fine.</v>

00:03:33.969 --> 00:03:37.819
<v Fiona Doyle>Have you put a deadline against that, or just the priority?</v>

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Just normal priority. No deadline set for that one.</v>

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.400
<v Hannah Price>Okay, got it. Separate entry from the alarm test.</v>

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:52.629
<v David Whitfield>And the near miss at the palletiser — that's a separate write-up as well, isn't it?</v>

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:03.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. We need someone to write up the near miss at the palletiser after lunch. It matters but it's not urgent. Anyone able to take that?</v>

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:10.460
<v Hannah Price>Um, I'm not volunteering for that as well. My yes was for the risk assessment.</v>

00:04:12.389 --> 00:04:17.990
<v David Whitfield>And I was only asking which bit of paperwork we meant. I'm not taking the write-up.</v>

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:20.680
<v Fiona Doyle>No taker, then. That's still unallocated.</v>

00:04:23.149 --> 00:04:30.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, it needs doing after lunch, but nobody owns it. Let's be clear about that rather than pretend it's covered.</v>

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.350
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. A quiet Teams call doesn't count as someone saying yes.</v>

00:04:35.629 --> 00:04:41.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. Davey, can you send the shift handover report round next Tuesday, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:04:42.819 --> 00:04:47.370
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round next Tuesday. Spare-minute job, understood.</v>

00:04:49.639 --> 00:04:53.139
<v Fiona Doyle>Next Tuesday for that one, not bundled into this afternoon?</v>

00:04:54.040 --> 00:05:00.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, next Tuesday. If you've got a spare minute — not something to bump the priority work for.</v>

00:05:02.269 --> 00:05:04.370
<v David Whitfield>Fine by me. I've got that.</v>

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.209
<v Jamie Brennan>More useful reading than the match report, anyway.</v>

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.009
<v David Whitfield>Low bar, mate. Very low bar.</v>

00:05:13.089 --> 00:05:16.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, quick read-back of what we've actually agreed, then we're done.</v>

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:24.870
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Mine's the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel, tomorrow at 9:30. Needs doing first because it's holding production up.</v>

00:05:26.439 --> 00:05:38.339
<v Hannah Price>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon — not an emergency, but no slipping it. And I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Palletiser at normal priority, no deadline set.</v>

00:05:39.209 --> 00:05:44.459
<v David Whitfield>I'll send the shift handover report round next Tuesday, if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:53.399
<v Fiona Doyle>And the near miss at the palletiser write-up is needed after lunch, matters but isn't urgent, and still has nobody against it.</v>

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:59.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. That's an open need, not an accepted task for anyone here.</v>

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:04.459
<v Jamie Brennan>Nothing assigned out of the forklifts rattle either. Observation only.</v>

00:06:06.339 --> 00:06:10.189
<v Fiona Doyle>And GT1 stays blocked on parts. No work agreed on that.</v>

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that's clear. Thanks, everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>
